            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0585" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg513"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10901.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Russian Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Russian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic">January 6,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor in
                    behalf of the Imperial Government to request the extradition of Jan Janov
                    Pouren, a Russian subject, charged with murder, robbery, and attempted murders,
                    and now at New York, where he lives under the name of W. Kohks, alias Martin
                    Martinson.</p>
                <p>The above man’s criminal record is in the hands of the consul general of Russia
                    at New York who, as agent of the Imperial Government <pb facs="0586" n="514"
                        xml:id="pg514"/> at New York, has charge of the proceedings before the local
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rosen.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
